{"chapter": "etale", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "025F", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-topological-etale}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:78577542bd0e3b46e957e70eec6a2efdf70fc32c356e311a32355bfb941afcdd", "source_text": "Topological properties of <ACCENT_0001>tale morphisms", "source_text_hash": "sha256:17065511441d8c7ea592b327fc051fd5ef3386832ee304a7687d50777f4cce9e", "unit_id": "tag:025F:title"}
{"chapter": "etale", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "025F", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "REF_0001": "\\cite[Expos\\'e I.5]{SGA1}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9d71f6bdf220303c95278717e54a5fdb830f0e65bf17c47981b9a0286814c6a7", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nWe present a few of the topological properties of <ACCENT_0001>tale and\nunramified morphisms. First, we give what Grothendieck\ncalls the <TEXTITOPEN_0001>fundamental property of <ACCENT_0002>tale morphisms<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>, see\n<REF_0001>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6b5c063f379b16579c62229c787ebf06157a0eb8adf783ddf9f8b13a5c9d66bd", "unit_id": "tag:025F:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "etale", "node_kind": "theorem", "parent_tag": "025F", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$f$", "MATH_0004": "$f$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{theorem}\n\\label{theorem-etale-radicial-open}\n", "suffix": "\\end{theorem}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:6dc777950cd17b31754fe353a6f530cb318c9a3dc0996b2f0e060e4535fc840c", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:fab9dd099e9fd6563ab747e873f66c5bd7aa221f7f88ee12d177fe7247cc5dea", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes.\nThe following are equivalent:\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0002> is an open immersion,\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0003> is universally injective and <ACCENT_0001>tale, and\n<STRUCT_0004> <MATH_0004> is a flat monomorphism, locally of finite presentation.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:10d52b3c9160085ffb0d860e434b0af435f1d1ec1f21b6f3f684030a8091de8f", "unit_id": "tag:025G:statement"}
{"chapter": "etale", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "025F", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0003": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$f$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$f$", "MATH_0004": "$f$", "MATH_0005": "$f$", "MATH_0006": "$Y$", "MATH_0007": "$f(X)$", "MATH_0008": "$f$", "MATH_0009": "$f$", "MATH_0010": "$f$", "MATH_0011": "$f$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{morphisms-lemma-open-immersion-etale}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{morphisms-lemma-etale-flat}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{morphisms-lemma-etale-locally-finite-presentation}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-universally-injective-unramified}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{morphisms-lemma-fppf-open}", "REF_0006": "\\ref{descent-lemma-flat-surjective-quasi-compact-monomorphism-isomorphism}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0002": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0003": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0004": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:85f9481b84b3d1000b3e261ffba31aad8134e7a8e19cea3171958353c61894ab", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0daae314e12dd39a6ecd221feebbd82d93feb6b6f83735ca24937a1c86eaffe4", "source_text": "An open immersion is universally injective\nsince any base change of an open immersion\nis an open immersion. Moreover, it is <ACCENT_0001>tale by\nMorphisms, Lemma <REF_0001>.\nHence (1) implies (2).\n\n<STRUCT_0001><STRUCT_0002>\nAssume <MATH_0001> is universally injective and <ACCENT_0002>tale.\nSince <MATH_0002> is <ACCENT_0003>tale it is flat and locally of finite presentation, see\nMorphisms, Lemmas <REF_0002> and\n<REF_0003>.\nBy\nLemma <REF_0004>\nwe see that <MATH_0003> is a monomorphism. Hence (2) implies (3).\n\n<STRUCT_0003><STRUCT_0004>\nAssume <MATH_0004> is flat, locally of finite presentation, and a monomorphism.\nThen <MATH_0005> is open, see\nMorphisms, Lemma <REF_0005>.\nThus we may replace <MATH_0006> by <MATH_0007> and we may assume <MATH_0008> is\nsurjective. Then <MATH_0009> is open and bijective hence a homeomorphism.\nHence <MATH_0010> is quasi-compact. Hence\nDescent, Lemma\n<REF_0006>\nshows that <MATH_0011> is an isomorphism and we win.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:cbb794828830ccbde9bc5eaee774ed433db0037164930564e11a30e779fad6e2", "unit_id": "tag:025G:proof"}
{"chapter": "etale", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "025F", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:00711db8de5e2314f91a7bec82c382c3c7c87e02a46d59241be4f4901492398e", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nHere is another result of a similar flavor.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:cf47cd29776ace862b4ed90367531621cbdcc049e4c63dbcc81a7b83cae39fb7", "unit_id": "tag:025F:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "etale", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "025F", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "FOOTNOTECLOSE_0001": "}", "FOOTNOTEOPEN_0001": "\\footnote{", "MATH_0001": "$\\pi : X \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$s \\in S$", "MATH_0003": "$\\pi$", "MATH_0004": "$\\pi$", "MATH_0005": "$\\pi^{-1}(\\{s\\}) = \\{x\\}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\kappa(s) \\subset \\kappa(x)$", "MATH_0007": "$\\kappa(s) = \\kappa(x)$", "MATH_0008": "$U$", "MATH_0009": "$s$", "MATH_0010": "$\\pi|_{\\pi^{-1}(U)} : \\pi^{-1}(U) \\to U$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\item", "STRUCT_0006": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-finite-etale-one-point}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ecae92e7316137128e917ccdfafe54fba22dc1102e25f68e91e6e920d6e1b94e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5c656861af778d296e5bc0b6313300e41c670ecdfc6c9e25aecd48a2cef7303a", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes. Let <MATH_0002>.\nAssume that\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0003> is finite,\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0004> is <ACCENT_0001>tale,\n<STRUCT_0004> <MATH_0005>, and\n<STRUCT_0005> <MATH_0006> is purely\ninseparable<FOOTNOTEOPEN_0001>In view of condition (2)\nthis is equivalent to <MATH_0007>.<FOOTNOTECLOSE_0001>.\n<STRUCT_0006>\nThen there exists an open neighbourhood <MATH_0008> of <MATH_0009> such that\n<MATH_0010> is an isomorphism.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:24acb15ad5b403fec61540554cb081bbdae3198c0574e192713841cb504fd515", "unit_id": "tag:04DH:statement"}
{"chapter": "etale", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "025F", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$U$", "MATH_0002": "$s$", "MATH_0003": "$\\pi|_{\\pi^{-1}(U)} : \\pi^{-1}(U) \\to U$", "MATH_0004": "$U$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-finite-unramified-one-point}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{theorem-etale-radicial-open}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d05f7e9b82093b670b2d5cdb946b510b4f8e91b1d727bda66d56fa05c9ffead0", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:dafbd07bb77a631b14b279d081d6208a9d151c99b5a1d19f75e96514818c3d0d", "source_text": "By\nLemma <REF_0001>\nthere exists an open neighbourhood <MATH_0001> of <MATH_0002> such that\n<MATH_0003> is a closed immersion.\nBut a morphism which is <ACCENT_0001>tale and a closed immersion is an\nopen immersion (for example by\nTheorem <REF_0002>).\nHence after shrinking <MATH_0004> we obtain an isomorphism.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:50195db7319240eb34b6b8743c317cce6af8d11482963a61388b6958fdf3ccb4", "unit_id": "tag:04DH:proof"}
{"chapter": "etale", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "025F", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$U \\to X$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$p$", "MATH_0004": "$F_{U/X} : U \\to U \\times_{X, F_X} X$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-relative-frobenius-etale}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:cd05750606c6fb8e5fa6a82e91dc7aa9be339be8517c991e352ce86893e276f5", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a73cc2174fc2198319b8a727995196f66baee6d5d2fea9339a23f41cd46d3a65", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be an <ACCENT_0001>tale morphism of schemes\nwhere <MATH_0002> is a scheme in characteristic <MATH_0003>.\nThen the relative Frobenius <MATH_0004>\nis an isomorphism.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:502a4c264b09224a09e42d478d49e9861ad0748f50bb3ecbabc48093a3c7345a", "unit_id": "tag:0EBS:statement"}
{"chapter": "etale", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "025F", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$F_{U/X}$", "MATH_0002": "$F_{U/X}$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$F_{U/X}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{varieties-lemma-relative-frobenius}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{morphisms-lemma-etale-permanence}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{theorem-etale-radicial-open}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:bce6982f3e0c7473818ae3434c6d8698b49ef102ceb79902f366e2d48e5ad022", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:48c3d25e9b2ea3675902be83423a03c2268fc6a70633a85724b5a131b7ab6aff", "source_text": "The morphism <MATH_0001> is a universal homeomorphism by\nVarieties, Lemma <REF_0001>.\nThe morphism <MATH_0002> is <ACCENT_0001>tale as a\nmorphism between schemes <ACCENT_0002>tale over <MATH_0003>\n(Morphisms, Lemma <REF_0002>).\nHence <MATH_0004> is an isomorphism by\nTheorem <REF_0003>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:eac1579558f66e737537111089621eb36cb6a40d0931c8ff726583a106583fb4", "unit_id": "tag:0EBS:proof"}
